Selection rule (reproducible without a script; this is what was run)
  1. Walk css/css-flexbox/ excluding any directory named crashtests (those are
     vendored separately in tests/wpt/css-flexbox-crashtests/).
  2. A file is a candidate if it has a <link> whose rel contains "match" or
     "mismatch". Read with an HTML tokenizer, not a regex.
  3. Drop the candidate if it is not .html/.htm (.xht, .xhtml, .svg), if it has
     rel=mismatch, or if it contains a <script> element or any attribute whose
     name starts with "on" (the same test reftest.rs's needs_script applies).
     Scripted tests are counted as dropped-scripted, in that order of checks.
  4. Resolve the single rel=match href against the test's own directory
     (absolute /css/css-flexbox/... hrefs resolve inside the module). A test
     with more than one match link would be dropped; there were none.
  5. Drop the pair if the reference is not .html/.htm, is outside
     css/css-flexbox/, is missing, or itself contains script or on* attributes
     (none did).
  6. Vendor the test, its reference (once if shared), and any file named by
     <link rel=stylesheet href>, <img src>, <source|video|audio|iframe|embed
     src> or <object data> in either, if that file exists inside css/css-flexbox/.

